>Lecture: My Lecture Title' \u2014 value = 'My Lecture Title' (chars up to '<'). Good. Note `\\s*:\\s*` \u2014 'Lecture: My' \u2192 ':' then ' '. Good.\n\nHmm \u2014 but wait: does the playlist part of the webpage interfere? The regex searches the whole webpage; '>Lecture' appears only in the h3. Good.\n\nTest 5:\n\n```python\ndef test_single_video_title_from_lesson_name_variable(monkeypatch):\n    webpage = (\n        'player.playlist = [{\"file\": \"https://example.com/hls/video4.m3u8\"}];'\n        \"var lessonName = 'Fallback Lesson Name';\"\n    )\n    ...\n    result = ie._real_extract(LESSON_URL)\n    assert result['title'] == 'Fallback Lesson Name'\n```\n\nRegex: `lessonName\\s*=\\s*([\"\\'])(?P<value>(?:(?!\\1).)+)\\1` \u2014 on \"var lessonName = 'Fallback Lesson Name';\" \u2192 matches; group(1) = \"'\"; value = 'Fallback Lesson Name'. Good.\n\nHmm \u2014 wait, in test 4 and 5, is there any '>Lecture' or 'lessonName' in the playlist part? No.\n\nBut careful in test 5: the first title regex `>Lecture\\s*:\\s*...` must NOT match \u2014 it doesn't. Then second matches. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 one thing I should double check: `_search_regex` with a tuple of patterns and `group='value'`: \n\n```python\n        if isinstance(pattern, (str, compat_str, compiled_regex_type)):\n            mobj = re.search(pattern, string, flags)\n        else:\n            for p in pattern:\n                mobj = re.search(p, string, flags)\n                if mobj:\n                    break\n```\n\nThen `if group is None: return next((g for g in mobj.groups() if g is not None)) else: return mobj.group(group)`. With group='value' \u2192 mobj.group('value'). Good.\n\nFor the lesson search (no group): `next((g for g in mobj.groups() if g is not None))` \u2014 for `window\\.lesson\\s*=\\s*({.+?})\\s*;` there's one group (the JSON). Good.\n\nFor the playlist regex: group 1 = the JSON array. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 the fake downloader and `_search_regex`'s `self._downloader.params.get('no_color')`. With _FakeDownloader, params={} \u2192 .get \u2192 None \u2192 `not None` \u2192 True \u2192 `compat_os_name != 'nt'` \u2192 then `sys.stderr.isatty()`. Under pytest, sys.stderr is captured \u2014 pytest's capture object has isatty() \u2192 returns False (CaptureIO is an io.TextIOWrapper over BytesIO; isatty \u2192 False). OK.\n\nBut hmm \u2014 what if pytest is run with `-s` and stderr is a tty? Then _name = colored name \u2014 harmless.\n\nEdge: `sys.stderr` could be None in some weird contexts (pythonw) \u2192 AttributeError. Not our concern.\n\nNow \u2014 `InfoExtractor.__init__` \u2014 let me confirm signature. I'll query. If it's `def __init__(self, downloader=None)`, then `LinuxAcademyIE(_FakeDownloader())` works.\n\nLet me also double-check `try_get` catches KeyError \u2014 query 'try_get'.\n\nAnd 'date_formats' + 'extract_timezone' for timestamp confidence.\n\nNext batch:\n- 'InfoExtractor.__init__'\n- 'try_get'\n- 'date_formats'\n- 'extract_timezone'\n- 'determine_protocol'\n\nThen finalize.\n\nActually, also let me reconsider: should I verify `LinuxAcademyIE` has no required __init__ override? The get_info('LinuxAcademyIE._real_extract') output showed the class with '...' \u2014 there might be `_LOGIN_URL` etc. but __init__ is inherited. Fine.\n\nOne more thing \u2014 the test file must not leave global state. We only create local objects and monkeypatch instance attributes. \n\nAlso \u2014 \"Write as little top-level code as possible\" \u2014 imports + constants + helper + tests. No main.\n\nLet me also think about whether to use `pytest.mark.parametrize` \u2014 not needed.\n\nNow, about `_assert_timestamp` helper \u2014 fine.\n\nWait, one more check on `unified_timestamp('2019-06-25')`: \n\n- `re.sub('[,|]', '', '2019-06-25')` \u2192 '2019-06-25'.\n- pm_delta: no 'PM' \u2192 0.\n- extract_timezone('2019-06-25') \u2014 searches for tz patterns; none \u2192 returns (timedelta(0)?, '2019-06-25')? Need to confirm extract_timezone's no-match behavio